# Development scratch layer -- NOT a profile and NOT a separate image.
#
# This list is an extra apt cache layer stacked on top of the profile layer,
# enabled with CHIRON_DEV_LAYER=1 when calling build-profile.sh. It exists for
# one reason: iterating on a package set in a temporary workspace used to cost
# a full apt run per attempt, because editing profiles/graphical/packages.list
# changes that layer's key and misses its cache -- twenty attempts, twenty
# multi-hour runs under qemu-user.
#
# With this layer, the profile layer underneath is untouched and keeps hitting
# its cache, so only what changes here is reinstalled.
#
#   # fast iteration in a throwaway workspace
#   CHIRON_DEV_LAYER=1 ./scripts/builder/build-profile.sh <workspace> graphical
#
#   # clean production build: leave the variable unset
#   ./scripts/builder/build-profile.sh <workspace> graphical
#
# The image is still <profile>.sqfs either way; this layer never renames it and
# never creates a profile of its own. Because the profile layer is saved
# separately and unmodified, the clean build restores the very tarball the dev
# builds were stacking on instead of starting cold.
#
# When something here proves itself, move it into the profile list it belongs
# to and empty it out again. Anything left here does NOT ship in a production
# image -- that is the point of the split, and also the trap: a package that is
# only ever tested from this layer has never been in an image the board runs.
#
# One package per line, comments with #. An empty list is valid and installs
# nothing.
